4. Number of candidates below 80th percentile in P: Number of candidates below 80th percentile in C: Number of candidates below 80th percentile in M = 4:2:1. BIE uses a different process for selection. If any candidate is appearing in the AET by AIE, BIE considers their AET score for final selection provided the candidate is at or above the 80th percentile in P. Any other candidate at or above the 80th percentile in P in CET, but who is not eligible for the AET, is required to appear in a separate test to be conducted by BIE for being considered for final selection. Altogether, there are 400 candidates this year who are at or above the 80th percentile in P.', options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2017 Slot 1, DILR Q11. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2017-Question-Paper-Slot-1-DILR/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2017-s1-dilr-q11';
