UPDATE questions SET topic = 'Tables & Caselets', prompt = 'How many elective courses among E1 to E6 had a decrease in their enrollments after the change process?', passage = 'There were seven elective courses - E1 to E7 - running in a specific term in a college. Each of the 300 students enrolled had chosen just one elective from among these seven. However, before the start of the term, E7 was withdrawn as the instructor concerned had left the college. The students who had opted for E7 were allowed to join any of the remaining electives. Also, the students who had chosen other electives were given one chance to change their choice. The table below captures the movement of the students from one elective to another during this process. Movement from one elective to the same elective simply means no movement. Some numbers in the table got accidentally erased; however, it is known that these were either 0 or 1. Further, the following are known:
1. Before the change process there were 6 more students in E1 than in E4, but after the reshuffle, the number of students in E4 was 3 more than that in E1.
2. The number of students in E2 increased by 30 after the change process.
3. Before the change process, E4 had 2 more students than E6, while E2 had 10 more students than E3.

[[img:/pyq/img/6b55de61ad0ad017.png]]', options = '["4", "1", "2", "3"]'::jsonb, explanation = 'Official CAT 2017 Slot 2, DILR Q5. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2017-Question-Paper-Slot-2-DILR/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2017-s2-dilr-q05';
