UPDATE questions SET topic = 'Para jumbles', prompt = 'The four sentences (labelled 1, 2, 3, and 4) given in this question, when properly sequenced, form a coherent paragraph. Decide on the proper order for the sentences and key in this sequence of four numbers as your answer. 1) The woodland’s canopy receives most of the sunlight that falls on the trees. 2) Swifts do not confine themselves to woodlands, but hunt wherever there are insects in the air. 3) With their streamlined bodies, swifts are agile flyers, ideally adapted to twisting and turning through the air as they chase flying insects - the creatures that form their staple diet. 4) Hundreds of thousands of insects fly in the sunshine up above the canopy, some falling prey to swifts and swallows', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2018 Slot 1, VARC Q20. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2018-Question-Paper-Slot-1-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2018-s1-varc-q20';
