2. Companies in many countries routinely engage in such activities which means that the employees are left with unpaid entitlements
3. Deliberate and systematic liquidation of a company to avoid liabilities and then restarting the business is called phoenixing.
4. The Australian Minister for Revenue and Services discovered in an audit that phoenixing had cost the Australian economy between $2.9bn and $5.1bn last year.', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2018 Slot 2, VARC Q26. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2018-Question-Paper-Slot-2-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2018-s2-varc-q26';
