UPDATE questions SET topic = 'Binary logic (truth/lie)', prompt = 'Considering all companies'' products, which product category had the highest revenue?', passage = 'Each of the 23 boxes in the picture below represents a product manufactured by one of the following three companies: Alfa, Bravo and Charlie. The area of a box is proportional to the revenue from the corresponding product, while its centre represents the Product popularity and Market potential scores of the product (out of 20). The shadings of some of the boxes have got erased. The companies classified their products into four categories based on a combination of scores (out of 20) on the two parameters - Product popularity and Market potential as given below: The following facts are known:

1. Alfa and Bravo had the same number of products in the Blockbuster category.
2. Charlie had more products than Bravo but fewer products than Alfa in the No-hope category.
3. Each company had an equal number of products in the Promising category.
4. Charlie did not have any product in the Doubtful category, while Alfa had one product more than Bravo in this category
5. Bravo had a higher revenue than Alfa from products in the Doubtful category.
6. Charlie had a higher revenue than Bravo from products in the Blockbuster category.
7. Bravo and Charlie had the same revenue from products in the No-hope category.
8. Alfa and Charlie had the same total revenue considering all products.

[[img:/pyq/img/d4ef7e83a6c71d94.png]]
[[img:/pyq/img/7599b2840a1dc48b.png]]', options = '["No-hope", "Blockbuster", "Doubtful", "Promising"]'::jsonb, explanation = 'Official CAT 2018 Slot 2, DILR Q21. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2018-Question-Paper-Slot-2-DILR/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2018-s2-dilr-q21';
UPDATE questions SET answer = '1' WHERE id = 'cat-2018-s2-dilr-q21' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM answer_key_corrections c WHERE c.question_id = 'cat-2018-s2-dilr-q21');
