UPDATE questions SET topic = 'Para jumbles', prompt = 'The four sentences (labelled 1, 2, 3, 4) given below, when properly sequenced would yield a coherent paragraph. Decide on the proper sequence of the order of the sentences and key in the sequence of the four numbers as your answer. 1. People with dyslexia have difficulty with print-reading, and people with autism spectrum disorder have difficulty with mind-reading. 2. An example of a lost cognitive instinct is mind-reading: our capacity to think of ourselves and others as having beliefs, desires, thoughts and feelings. 3. Mind-reading looks increasingly like literacy, a skill we know for sure is not in our genes, since scripts have been around for only 5,000-6,000 years. 4. Print-reading, like mind-reading varies across cultures, depends heavily on certain parts of the brain, and is subject to developmental disorders.', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2019 Slot 1, VARC Q21. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2019-Question-Paper-Slot-1-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2019-s1-varc-q21';
