3. This configuration enables one to distinguish an astronaut on the Moon.
4. When these are combined with the large telescopes, they produce what is called interferometry: a simulation of the power of a mirror 16 m in diameter and the resolution of a telescope of 200 m.', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2020 Slot 2, VARC Q1. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2020-Question-Paper-Slot-2-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2020-s2-varc-q01';
