een called the "auxiliary sciences" of history—archaeology, epigraphy, numismatics, chronology, and so forth. . . . The second observation is that the necessity to establish these basic facts rests not on any quality in the facts themselves, but on an apriori decision of the historian. In spite of C. P. Scott''s motto, every journalist knows today that the most effective way to influence opinion is by the selection and arrangement of the appropriate facts. It used to be said that facts speak for themselves. This is, of course, untrue. The facts speak only when the historian calls on them: it is he who decides to which facts to give the floor, and in what order or context. . . . The only reason why we are interested to know that the battle was fought at Hastings in 1066 is that historians regard it as a major historical event. . . . Professor Talcott Parsons once called [science] "a selective system of cognitive orientations to reality." It might perhaps have been put more simply. But history is, among other things, that. The historian is necessarily selective. The belief in a hard core of historical facts existing objectively and independently of the interpretation of the historian is a preposterous fallacy, but one which it is very hard to eradicate.', options = '["the truth value of a fact is independent of the historian who expresses it.", "a fact, by its very nature, is objective and universal, irrespective of the context in which it is placed.", "facts, like truth, can be relative: what is fact for person X may not be so for person Y.", "the order in which a series of facts is presented does not have any bearing on the production of meaning."]'::jsonb, explanation = 'Official CAT 2023 Slot 2, VARC Q2. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2023-Question-Paper-Slot-2-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2023-s2-varc-q02';
UPDATE questions SET answer = '2' WHERE id = 'cat-2023-s2-varc-q02' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM answer_key_corrections c WHERE c.question_id = 'cat-2023-s2-varc-q02');
