1. No known real researcher of human behaviour would say that gender is all nature or all nurture. 2. The evidence for a biological basis for gender certainly doesn’t mean we should be complacent in the face of sexism. 3. Many people are uncomfortable with the idea that gender is not purely a social construct. 4. Despite this empirical truth, researchers who study the biological basis of gender often face political pushback. 5. There’s a political preference for gender to be only a reflection of social factors and so entirely malleable.', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2024 Slot 2, VARC Q24. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2024-Question-Paper-Slot-2-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2024-s2-varc-q24';
