3. Inasmuch as photography is an ellipse of language and a condensation of an ‘ineffable’ social whole, it constitutes an anti- intellectual weapon and tends to spirit away ‘politics’ (that is to say a body of problems and solutions) to the advantage of a ''manner of being'', a socio-moral status.
4. Photography tends to restore the paternalistic nature of elections, whose elitist essence has been disrupted by proportional representation and the rule of parties (the Right seems to use it more than the Left).', passage = NULL, options = NULL, explanation = 'Official CAT 2025 Slot 3, VARC Q1. Answer key cross-checked against https://online.2iim.com/CAT-question-paper/CAT-2025-Question-Paper-Slot-3-VARC/', has_figure = FALSE WHERE id = 'cat-2025-s3-varc-q01';
